cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Sester in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Sester: metering, quota, fail-closed policy and verifiable receipts for AI-agent APIs"
authors:
  - alias: goun7
    website: "https://github.com/goun7"
version: 0.6.1
date-released: "2026-09-14"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/goun7/Sester"
url: "https://pypi.org/project/sester/"
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - metering
  - payments
  - x402
  - asgi-middleware
  - fintech
abstract: >-
  Sester is a single ASGI middleware that plugs x402-style metering,
  quotas, fail-closed spend policy and a tamper-evident hash-chain
  receipt ledger into AI-agent APIs. Four agent-commerce protocols
  (x402, AP2, ACP, UCP) compile onto one wire-format core, and every
  charge or denial produces evidence a third party can verify with
  nothing but sha256.
